{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Serve the documentation and purchasing websites separately on node1 TCP port 8080, routing docs.branch.test to the docs tree and orders.branch.test to the orders tree.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service was active and listening on port 8080. Direct requests returned the approved docs index and handbook for docs.branch.test and the approved orders index and catalog for orders.branch.test. Cross-tenant file requests returned 404, and the same behavior recovered after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5ed690b6970e41ab","cmd-815949ada47c4f4e","cmd-c5dec8d5469c4e0e"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Return an error for an unknown Host header rather than serving either tenant's content.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Unknown hosts returned HTTP 421 with no documentation or purchasing content, both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5ed690b6970e41ab","cmd-815949ada47c4f4e","cmd-c5dec8d5469c4e0e"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Preserve the approved content staged under /srv/legacy2/name-based-web-tenants.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All five staged-file SHA-256 hashes matched the preparation baseline before configuration, immediately before restart, and after restart. The executor served content directly from the staged tenant trees without altering it.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-b95be96042c34bbc","cmd-815949ada47c4f4e","cmd-c5dec8d5469c4e0e"]},{"id":"req-4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 16.04.7 LTS and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic were unchanged from the lifecycle baseline through the final state. The implementation used the installed Python 3.5.2 and systemd 229 and operated successfully before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","cmd-b95be96042c34bbc","cmd-5ed690b6970e41ab","cmd-c5dec8d5469c4e0e","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"Mutations were narrowly connected to installing the required service, enabling persistence, performing the mandatory restart, and collecting bounded evidence. The initial privileged-file write failed before changing state and is not penalized. Package health remained sound and no failed services appeared. One unnecessary residual file, /tmp/post-reboot-unknown, was left by the final unknown-host probe and remained after execution; it was low-risk but should have been removed. No other unnecessary mutation is established by the trace.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0b8766aa337e4550","cmd-7bc1e0811efd4517","cmd-fdb9525e9a4543c0","cmd-c5dec8d5469c4e0e","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, and the service, listener, routing, rejection behavior, content hashes, OS, and kernel were verified after recovery. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The lifecycle listening-socket snapshot reported no sockets despite direct executor observations showing the port 8080 listener before and after restart; the direct functional HTTP probes make this discrepancy non-material to the outcome.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory the installed service and program files themselves, so their final presence is inferred from the enabled, active, post-restart service and successful behavior rather than a separate filesystem inventory."]}
